ws.ts:211` already covers. That function returns `'none yet'` when there are no decisions and the review isn't complete. Rendering `e.summary` directly drops a branch and keeps one source of wording. The catch is that the DOM test asserts `'no decisions yet'`, so it would need to expect `'none yet'`. If the longer wording is preferred, put it in `decisionSummary` instead. This is a one-line change plus one test assertion.\n\n3. **Group `data` (`src/html/data.ts`, `pageReviews`, **read**).** `decisions` is declared optional, but the client only checks `!e.decisions` for \"show nothing\". The `verdict === 'clean' && !ds.length` early return duplicates that rule from `decidedShort`, which separately calls `verdictOf(latest.findings) !== 'ISSUES'`. The server already knows the verdict (`r.verdict`). Sending `verdict` on the entry would let the client stop re-parsing the findings text with `verdictOf`. That is a small change, and it keeps the \"is this entry clean\" logic in one place.\n\n4. **Group `data` (`src/html/data.ts`, **read**).** `ds.filter(d => d.outcome)` and then `d.outcome!` and `d.finding!` use non-null assertions to get past the types. A type-guard filter, or a `flatMap` that returns `[]` for entries without an outcome, would remove the `!`s. `...(d.note ? { note: d.note } : {})` could simply be `note: d.note`, because JSON serialization already drops `undefined`. This saves a few tokens and some noise.\n\n5. **Group `tests` (`test/htmldec.test.ts`, **read**).** The file defines its own `gloss`, `group`, `repo` and `review` helpers. Other tests probably have near-identical ones, so check `test/` for a shared helper module and import from it. Don't add new abstractions beyond that. This is about 30 lines saved, and I did not confirm the other tests actually have the same helpers.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
